{
  "_readme": "Games whose developers or publishers disclosed real unit sales publicly. Seeded from the sample Gamalytic published alongside its accuracy benchmark, so our numbers are comparable to theirs. `reportedAt` is when the figure was announced. `snapshot` freezes the estimator inputs as of that date; where it is null the harness falls back to live review counts, which biases results — see the warning the harness prints. Snapshots are now filled for every row from `store.steampowered.com/appreviewhistogram/<appid>`, which returns per-bucket review counts for a game's whole life and so gives the review count and positive share on the day of the disclosure. That histogram counts Steam purchasers and excludes externally-activated keys, while the extension reads `appreviews` with `purchase_type=all`; `snapshot.reviews` is therefore the historical histogram count scaled by `k`, today's ratio between the two populations for that game. `reviewsAsRead` keeps every raw number so the scaling can be checked or undone. `k` runs 0.75 to 1.69 across these games and tracks key giveaways, so it is an estimate and not a measurement.",
  "_schema": {
    "appId": "Steam app id",
    "name": "display name",
    "reportedUnits": "units sold as publicly disclosed",
    "reportedAt": "ISO date of the disclosure",
    "snapshot": "optional frozen inputs: { reviews, positivePct, listPrice, releaseYear, isFree, tags }",
    "source": "URL of the disclosure, for rows gathered after the original thirty",
    "quote": "the sentence the figure was read from",
    "scopeNote": "how confident the collector was that the figure is Steam units rather than all platforms",
    "foundBy": "which search produced the row",
    "reviewsAsRead": "raw histogram and API review counts behind `snapshot.reviews`, and the k that scaled them"
  },
